messages:
Amanda Chen: Hey — sketching a 'grace wallet' idea for routing/quota. free/pro/enterprise get different wallet sizes per-region. wallets let us route to cheaper variants without failing the request.

Ron Patel: Nice. wallets = burst credits? how are they refilled?

Amanda Chen: refill rules: time-window accrual + top-up on billing events. fallback ladder uses wallet first, then plan quota, then hard deny.

Suresh Iyer: Important: variant fallback order should be deterministic. propose: 1) quantized-compatible model (same arch), 2) reduced-context variant, 3) lower-llm-size fallback, 4) error. Also attach telemetry tags so we can track quality regressions.

Lina Gomez: Console UX note — expose wallet balance per-region and a 'simulate fallback' toggle for canary customers.

Ron Patel: API shape? something like:
```json
{
  "policy_version": "2026-03-01",
  "tiers": {
    "free": {
      "wallet": {
        "region": "auto",
        "size_tokens": 1000,
        "refill_rate_per_hour": 50
      },
      "fallback_order": ["q8_compat", "short_ctx", "small_model"]
    },
    "pro": {
      "wallet": {
        "region": "auto",
        "size_tokens": 10000,
        "refill_rate_per_hour": 500
      },
      "fallback_order": ["q8_compat", "q4_compat", "short_ctx", "small_model"]
    },
    "enterprise": {
      "wallet": {
        "region": "pinned",
        "size_tokens": 100000,
        "refill_rate_per_hour": 5000
      },
      "fallback_order": ["q8_compat", "q4_compat", "full_ctx_small_model"]
    }
  }
}
```

Amanda Chen: yeah that plus per-tenant overrides via console. question: should wallet be consumed on a per-token or per-invocation basis? per-token gives more granular control.

Suresh Iyer: Per-token preferred. Also need guardrail to avoid wallets being used for long-running streaming sessions — cap per-stream wallet draw.

deploy-bot: [deploy-started] policy-service v2.3 rolling to staging

Ron Patel: telemetry hooks: increment counters: wallet_used, fallback_variant, final_status. link them to prompt sets so evals can detect regressions.

Lina Gomez: UI: show 'fallback rate' sparkline and links to example requests that fell back (anonymized). product wants an SLA-impact metric.

Amanda Chen: ops question — if regional wallet empty, should we borrow from global pool? i lean yes, but with higher penalty so it shows up in billing.

Suresh Iyer: borrow with 'overdraft' flag. record in billing events. also add a hard ceiling per-tenant to prevent cost blowouts.

Ron Patel: OK next steps: PR for API schema, add unit tests for wallet accounting, add telemetry, and a canary rollout. I'll pick up PR for schema.

Amanda Chen: thanks. I'll mock the console panels and make a quick proto for the simulate toggle.

Lina Gomez: I'll prep a short runbook for ops — how to detect runaway fallbacks and reset wallets if needed.

Amanda Chen: filing RFC in docs repo after PR. good sync :thumbsup:
